WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0121: the pacing waits on the main thread (on top of 0001-0120).

wait_packet (0013) and idle_limit (0039) sleep inside a Bevy system. Bevy's render thread, while it waits
for the next render app, runs main-world tasks from the compute pool; when it took wait_packet it slept until
BG3's next packet before rendering the frame BG3 was waiting for. BG3's lockstep (wdlock) then timed out at
40 ms on about one frame in nine and showed the WoW frame before: the jerk when the camera turns. A
NonSendMarker keeps both waits on the main thread.

